===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*arsaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₃érsos}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ors-}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|ers|lang=ofs}} (West Frisian {{term|ears|lang=fy}}), Old Saxon {{term|ars|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|ars|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Arsch|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|ars|lang=non}}, {{term|rass|lang=non}} (Icelandic and Norwegian {{term|rass|lang=is}}), and more distantly with Old Armenian {{term|ոռ||tr=oṙ|ass|lang=xcl}}, and (Modern) Greek {{term|ουρά||tail|lang=el}}.

===Pronunciation===
